# PHASE 3 (step 3.4): run api-requests/auth0/get-token.http first - it stores the Auth0 token in {{token}}
# (it replaces auth-service/login.http). DELETE needs delete:patients, which the test app does not have -> 403.
### PHASE 0 (step 0.10): fixed (audit B10) - the request had NO Authorization header,
# so the gateway always answered 401. Run auth-service/login.http first.
#
# PHASE 0 (old):
# POST http://localhost:4004/api/patients
# Content-Type: application/json
#
# { "name": "user ", "email": "user.test@example.com", "address": "123 Main St, Frankfurt, Germany",
#   "birthDate": "1998-04-23", "registrationDate": "2025-01-01" }

### Create a patient -> 201 (run twice -> 409 Conflict, same email)
POST http://localhost:4004/api/patients
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "user ",
  "email": "user.test@example.com",
  "address": "123 Main St, Frankfurt, Germany",
  "birthDate": "1998-04-23",
  "registrationDate": "2025-01-01"
}

### Invalid input -> 400 with an "errors" map per field
POST http://localhost:4004/api/patients
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

{
  "name": "",
  "email": "not-an-email",
  "address": "X",
  "birthDate": "2999-01-01",
  "registrationDate": "2025-01-01"
}
